{
  "reason": "Use Tier 2: add cross-view prediction consistency to the existing masked transformer’s objective. Bidirectional reconstruction achieved 0.5800, while separating prediction and reconstruction views fell to 0.5463 and adding local convolution reached only 0.5725. These results suggest testing whether the two views need explicit representation alignment, although they do not establish the cause of the decline.",
  "module": [
    "model_design",
    "training_evaluation"
  ],
  "plan": {
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering": null,
    "model_design": "Make one controlled objective change: add clean-to-corrupted final-query consistency while retaining the supplied two-view architecture and supervised losses. Compute final-query logits for both views using the same tied item_emb, jointly trained item_bias, positive target, and existing 256 sampled negatives; add 0.1 times temperature-squared KL divergence with temperature 2, detaching the clean-view probability distribution. This tests whether auxiliary reconstruction can preserve next-item preferences despite historical masking, without adding independently fitted predictors or changing negative sampling. Preserve MaskedSASRec, its constructor, forward(self, sequence), predict(self, sequence, candidates), existing parameter names, and inference scoring.",
    "training_evaluation": "In train_one, retain both views’ final features from the shared forward pass and calculate the consistency term separately from the unchanged final-position and historical reconstruction losses. When an auxiliary view has no historical masks, skip its consistency term; preserve sampling, optimizer, hyperparameters, seed 42, validation candidates, checkpoint selection, and stopping rules to isolate the objective change. Preserve write_predict_script and its routing interface, strictly loading exactly one selected checkpoint per category, and verify exported scores match the selected model. Keep DATA_DIR=os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], supplied splits, all four categories, trial-local artifacts, and single-GPU execution; report measured macro validation HR@10 and leave hidden-test inference to the host."
  }
